# Protocol Buffers Rules

## Directory Structure

- All proto files must be stored in the `proto/` directory
- Follow proper namespace/package organization
- Version APIs properly in directory structure (v1, v2, etc.)
- Use meaningful file names that reflect the content

## Encoding Requirements

- Use UTF-8 encoding for all proto files
- Remove UTF-8 BOM if present
- Use Unix (LF) line endings, not Windows (CRLF)
- Begin files with `syntax = "proto3";` declaration

## Naming Conventions

- Use `snake_case` for field names
- Use `PascalCase` for message and service names
- Use `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for enum values
- Prefix enum values with the enum name to avoid collisions

## Code Generation

- Use `buf` for validation and code generation
- Configure output directories explicitly
- Set proper languages and options
- Never modify generated code manually

## Buffer Structure

- Split different resources into separate proto files
- Group related messages in the same file
- Keep dependencies between proto files minimal
- Use imports judiciously

## API Design

- Define service interfaces clearly
- Use explicit request/response messages
- Implement pagination for list operations
- Document all fields with clear comments 